# Pick ONE way to point the backend at the Prism database.
# The backend only ever runs SELECTs — it cannot modify Prism.

# (A) easiest: read creds from the Prism install/dump folder at runtime
# (the folder holding Model.dll.config + DBList.txt)
PRISM_CONFIG_DIR=/path/to/PRISM_PLUS

# (B) or a full DSN
# PRISM_DSN=sqlserver://user:pass@db-host:1433?database=PRISM_PLUS

# (C) or individual vars
# PRISM_DB_SERVER=db-host
# PRISM_DB_USER=...
# PRISM_DB_PASSWORD=...
# PRISM_DB_DATABASE=PRISM_PLUS

# listen address (optional)
PRISM_UI_ADDR=:8080

# (optional) live CRM enrichment — read-only Postgres. Keep the read-only option:
# PRISM_CRM_DSN=postgresql://USER:PASS@crm-db-host:5432/crm?sslmode=require&options=-c%20default_transaction_read_only%3Don

# ---- push to a CRM (optional) ------------------------------------------
# Prism's database is only reachable from the office network, so this service
# PUSHES a full snapshot (units, deals, cancellations, people, agents,
# agencies) to the CRM on a timer. Outbound HTTPS only; nothing is exposed.
# Both must be set for the sync to run. The key is whatever the CRM has in
# PRISM_INGEST_KEY (generate with: openssl rand -hex 32).
# CRM_INGEST_URL=https://crm.example.com/api/integrations/prism/snapshot
# CRM_INGEST_KEY=
# SYNC_INTERVAL=10m          # Go duration; default 10m
# CRM_INGEST_DRY_RUN=1       # ask the CRM to report the diff without writing

# Where the built frontend lives. Auto-detected at ../frontend/dist when
# present, so `npm run build` in frontend/ is enough to serve the UI on :8080.
# PRISM_UI_STATIC=/path/to/frontend/dist

# Commission settings (agents, rates, rules, what was paid) — a local JSON
# file, the only thing this service writes. Default: ./commissions.json
# PRISM_COMMISSIONS_FILE=/var/lib/prism-ui/commissions.json
# Agents to track when that file is first created, by first name as Prism
# spells them (comma-separated; Turkish letters and case don't matter).
# PRISM_COMMISSIONS_SEED=ayse,mehmet
